---
description: Mandatory request routing before workflow prompts
alwaysApply: true
---

Before any stage prompt, follow `_ask/policies/workflow.md#request-route-gate`: classify each outcome as feature, bug fix, investigation, review, or behavior-preserving maintenance. State its route and evidence; separate mixed outcomes. Reproduce reported defects before regression tests or production changes. Direct stage commands retain this gate.

Use `_ask/policies/workflow.md#explore-and-grill-entry` for missing facts versus unresolved goals/tradeoffs, and `#intent-approval-and-specification-authority` for supported elaboration versus human product decisions. Apply route-specific artifacts and completion; research/review findings alone do not authorize implementation.

Route uncertainty through `_ask/policies/workflow.md#model-confidence-escalation` and diagnose failed checks under `_ask/policies/verification.md#failure-diagnosis`. `/off-path` applies only to this chat; request routing, reproduction, scope, and evidence rules remain in force.
